  "collision_model_note": "Collision-free is defined against a sampled env point cloud, which is a Monte Carlo stand-in for a true mesh-mesh test. A placement grazing an obstacle can pass one draw and fail another. Measured rate: 3 of 104000 placements (0.003%) flagged by one independent 50k redraw; three further 3-cloud audit passes replaced 9 more pairs. Expect roughly 0.008% of placements to be draw-dependent. Root cause: generate_valid_pairs measures clearance against the 10k dataset cloud, whose point spacing is the same order as offset=0.02, so that estimate carries error comparable to the threshold. To eliminate rather than reduce it, regenerate with --num_env_points 50000+. The pre-existing testing_data/ sets have the same property (the RRT-Connect baseline found 0-2 invalid endpoints per config on them).",
